      "writtenOn": "2018-06-18T23:18:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The BC1.2 chip uses the ID pin to sense if it is grounded to identify if it is an OTG device. However, the ID pin has no way to connect to the Type-C connector. As a result, the BC1.2 only recognizes it as a SDP. Seems impossible to differentiate an OTG device from a real SDP device, which should mux to the hub.",
      "parentUuid": "0ee0283d_8e77e295",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "4444c3d921a1720bb1dbd660045a652f8b1a765c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3afe23bb_38257781",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-21T20:07:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I try to list all the cases (any missing case?):\n 1) Type-C charger w/ PD: UFP, exclude it using USB-comm-capable bit -\u003e negative\n 2) Type-C charger w/o PD: UFP, we can\u0027t differentiate it with (5) -\u003e false-positive\n 3) Type-C device: DFP -\u003e negative\n 4) C-to-C to workstation: UFP -\u003e positive\n 5) Type-C hub and C-to-C to workstation: DFP -\u003e false-negative\n 6) C-to-A to BC1.2 charger: UFP, exclude it by checking BC1.2 chip -\u003e negative\n 7) C-to-A to workstation: UFP -\u003e positive\n 8) C-to-A female and A-to-A to BC1.2 charger: DFP -\u003e negative\n 9) C-to-A female and A-to-A to workstation: DFP, we want it mux to AP but can\u0027t differentiate it from (10) -\u003e false-negative\n 10) C-to-A female to USB device: DFP -\u003e negative\n 11) C-to-B-micro and B-to-A to workstation: UFP -\u003e positive\n 12a) C-to-B-micro and OTG cable to USB device: DFP -\u003e negative (if the C-to-B-micro adapter supports OTG detection)\n 12b) C-to-B-micro and OTG cable to USB device: UFP -\u003e false-positive (if the C-to-B-micro adapter doesn\u0027t support OTG detection)\n\nNote: \"negative\" means muxing to the hub correctly; \"positive\" means muxing to AP correctly; \"false-\" means muxing incorrectly.\n\nWe can also filter the case (4) out by checking the BC1.2 chip as amstan@ suggested. Will update the patch. So the remaining failure cases are:\n * false-positive on (2), (12b)\n * false-negative on (5), (7)\n\nWe may ignore the cases (5), (7), and (12b) as they are rare setup. And ask users to unplug the case (2). Does it make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "c593729f_a6bb9a09",
